    "body": "> For me, gitstatus (based on libgit2) has been orders of magnitude faster\r\n\r\n[gitstatus](https://github.com/romkatv/gitstatus) is a considerable rewrite of git status fetching implemented in libgit2. Unfortunately, libgit2 is simply slower than `git` on its own: https://github.com/libgit2/libgit2/issues/4230\r\n\r\n> Does Starship maintain a daemon in the background, like gitstatus?\r\n\r\nNot for the time being, no. We've discussed the possibility among maintainers, but it's not likely to happen in the near future.",
