    "body": "> > For me, gitstatus (based on libgit2) has been orders of magnitude faster\r\n> \r\n> [gitstatus](https://github.com/romkatv/gitstatus) is a considerable rewrite of git status fetching implemented in libgit2. Unfortunately, libgit2 is simply slower than `git` on its own: [libgit2/libgit2#4230](https://github.com/libgit2/libgit2/issues/4230)\r\n\r\nHas using [the gitstatus libgit2 fork](https://github.com/romkatv/libgit2) (I assume that's it) instead of upstream libgit2 ever been attempted?\r\n",
