    "updated_at": "2020-07-10T19:46:46Z",
    "body": "I tested it with hyperfine. After changing it tests still pass. \r\n\r\nIn a lightly modified starship repo it performs a bit better:\r\n| Command | Mean [ms] | Min [ms] | Max [ms] | Relative |\r\n|:---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\r\n| `starship module git_status` | 27.1 ± 5.2 | 17.8 | 36.9 | 4.71 ± 1.30 |\r\n| `starship_mod module git_status` | 21.2 ± 7.6 | 10.4 | 46.6 | 3.68 ± 1.52 |\r\n| `git status --porcelain` | 5.7 ± 1.1 | 3.3 | 16.7 | 1.00 |\r\n\r\nIn a chromium repo it actually performs a lot worse:\r\n| Command | Mean [s] | Min [s] | Max [s] | Relative |\r\n|:---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\r\n| `starship module git_status` | 3.624 ± 0.056 | 3.553 | 3.742 | 2.40 ± 0.07 |\r\n| `starship_mod module git_status` | 10.420 ± 2.047 | 7.682 | 13.767 | 6.91 ± 1.37 |\r\n| `git status --porcelain` | 1.507 ± 0.040 | 1.451 | 1.566 | 1.00 |\r\n\r\nIt looks like `git status`  is still the best choice.\r\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
