    "updated_at": "2020-07-11T14:52:00Z",
    "body": "I built `starship_mod` with `master` but on the `v0.44` tag the performance regression goes away. It looks like on `master` the `git_status` module is significantly slower.\r\n\r\nTested with `git2-rs` repo:\r\n| Command | Mean [ms] | Min [ms] | Max [ms] | Relative |\r\n|:---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\r\n| `starship module git_status` | 158.5 ± 4.9 | 155.5 | 177.5 | 2.36 ± 0.08 |\r\n| `starship_mod_v0.44 module git_status` | 158.7 ± 3.4 | 153.7 | 168.4 | 2.37 ± 0.07 |\r\n| `starship_mod_master module git_status` | 445.6 ± 67.9 | 315.1 | 488.3 | 6.64 ± 1.02 |\r\n| `starship_master module git_status` | 379.0 ± 81.0 | 312.7 | 477.0 | 5.65 ± 1.21 |\r\n| `git status --porcelain` | 67.1 ± 1.2 | 65.3 | 69.6 | 1.00 |\r\n\r\n\r\nTested with `chromium` repo:\r\n| Command | Mean [s] | Min [s] | Max [s] | Relative |\r\n|:---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\r\n| `starship module git_status` | 3.853 ± 0.024 | 3.818 | 3.896 | 2.58 ± 0.02 |\r\n| `starship_mod_v0.44 module git_status` | 3.868 ± 0.023 | 3.838 | 3.900 | 2.59 ± 0.02 |\r\n| `starship_mod_master module git_status` | 8.488 ± 1.642 | 7.633 | 11.625 | 5.68 ± 1.10 |\r\n| `starship_master module git_status` | 10.147 ± 2.056 | 7.716 | 11.890 | 6.79 ± 1.38 |\r\n| `git status --porcelain` | 1.495 ± 0.008 | 1.487 | 1.509 | 1.00 |\r\n\r\nTested with `starship` repo:\r\n| Command | Mean [ms] | Min [ms] | Max [ms] | Relative |\r\n|:---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\r\n| `starship module git_status` | 7.8 ± 0.5 | 7.2 | 10.7 | 1.72 ± 0.24 |\r\n| `starship_mod_v0.44 module git_status` | 7.8 ± 0.5 | 7.2 | 11.7 | 1.73 ± 0.25 |\r\n| `starship_mod_master module git_status` | 19.6 ± 3.9 | 13.7 | 27.9 | 4.34 ± 1.03 |\r\n| `starship_master module git_status` | 20.6 ± 3.8 | 13.5 | 30.0 | 4.56 ± 1.02 |\r\n| `git status --porcelain` | 4.5 ± 0.6 | 3.9 | 10.2 | 1.00 |\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n ",
