    "updated_at": "2020-10-14T18:35:32Z",
    "body": "> EDIT: Given it's a non-Rust binary, this might be a better fit as an alternate git module that interested users can configure. This avoids the complexity of bundling this in all custom releases to maintain cross-platform compatibility. Any thoughts?\r\n\r\nThe idea of having a `libgit` and a `gitstatus` module seems like the right approach to add `gitstatus`. That way git works by default, but if a user wants to they can compile `gitstatus` themselves and point to it in config. \r\n\r\nAlso, I've just written some [rust bindings](https://docs.rs/gitstatusd/0.2.1/gitstatusd/) for `gitstatus`. Their quite early on, but hopefully their helpfull.",
