    "created_at": "2020-12-20T20:02:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-12-20T20:05:08Z",
    "body": "To go in a completely different direction: what about porting https://github.com/starship/starship/discussions/1252#discussioncomment-58920 (spaceships git_status module) to rust: do one call to `git status --porcelain -b 2> /dev/null` and then du whatever the equivalent of `echo $output | grep ...` is in rust to try to fill as many of the current features in https://github.com/starship/starship/blob/master/src/modules/git_status.rs#L116 as possible. It might lead to some removed features, but most should be there (not sure yet, most of `GitStatusInfo` looks fairly doable). \r\n\r\nWould that be acceptable?\r\n\r\nRipping out libgit in other place is then another matter...",
